# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 219-221 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 16 — CHAPTERS 19-21, LEAN, 2026-09-24; RUN 2): both parents living and the mother fit
# for the father, the elders of his city at the gate, the one flogged before you and a dead parent, the five disabilities and the two courts, meat and wine
# with Proverbs' remembrance (219); the city's men by a deputation, stones and stone, R. Yose's tartemar and half-log and the deaths of the wicked and the
# righteous, purge the evildoers (220); a man hanged not a woman with R. Eliezer's Ashkelon, the reviler's analogy and not alive as the kingdom does, him
# alone and not two in a day, the uprooted tree buried with him, the overnight prohibition and the burial command with the dignity exception, the two
# commandments and the hanging at dusk, the curse of the Name, naked and the cloths, the court warned (221). Every row READ WHOLE; the cuts by
# ch19_ink.SP_. Sitting 15's form.
from ch19_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(219, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HIS FATHER AND HIS MOTHER SHALL SEIZE HIM" (21:19) — HE IS NOT LIABLE UNLESS HE HAS A FATHER AND A MOTHER (R. MEIR); R. JUDAH: IF HIS MOTHER WAS NOT FIT FOR HIS FATHER, HE DOES NOT BECOME A STUBBORN AND REBELLIOUS SON. ({SP_(219, 1, "שאינו", "חיב", "עד", "שיהיו", "לו", "אב", "ואם")} "that he is not liable until he has a father and a mother"; {SP_(219, 1, "אם", "לא", "היתה", "אמו", "ראויה", "לאביו")} "if his mother was not fit for his father"; {SP_(219, 1, "אינו", "נעשה", "בן", "סורר", "ומורה")} "he does not become a stubborn and rebellious son"): BOTH PARENTS A CONDITION (Sanhedrin 8:4 the answer sheet), R. Judah\'s "fit" the Mishnah\'s "if his mother was not like his father" (in voice, look and height — the Talmud\'s reading, not opened) — the compile\'s parent conditions with the dispute. Fresh.')
srow(219, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND BRING HIM OUT TO THE ELDERS OF HIS CITY AND TO THE GATE OF HIS PLACE" — THE OBLIGATION IS ON THE ELDERS OF HIS CITY AND AT THE GATE OF HIS PLACE. ({SP_(219, 2, "מצוה", "בזקני", "עירו", "ובשער", "מקומו")} "the obligation is on the elders of his city and at the gate of his place"): the local court (207:1\'s form) — the compile\'s venue. Fresh.')
srow(219, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THEY SHALL SAY TO THE ELDERS OF HIS CITY: THIS SON OF OURS" (21:20) — THIS IS THE ONE FLOGGED BEFORE YOU; IT TEACHES THAT IF ONE OF THEM DIED HE IS NOT STONED. ({SP_(219, 3, "זהו", "שלקה", "בפניכם")} "this is the one who was flogged before you"; {SP_(219, 3, "שאם", "מת", "אחד", "מהם", "אינו", "נסקל")} "that if one of them died he is not stoned"): "THIS" THE FLOGGED ONE (the same court, 219:4), "OURS" BOTH PARENTS ALIVE at the second trial — the compile\'s sequence condition. Fresh.')
srow(219, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'IF ONE OF THEM WAS MAIMED, LAME, MUTE, BLIND OR DEAF, HE DOES NOT BECOME A STUBBORN AND REBELLIOUS SON: "SEIZE" NOT THE MAIMED, "BRING OUT" NOT THE LAME, "SAY" NOT THE MUTE, "THIS SON OF OURS" NOT THE BLIND, "HE DOES NOT HEED OUR VOICE" NOT THE DEAF. THEY WARN HIM BEFORE THREE AND FLOG HIM; IF HE REPEATED, HE IS JUDGED BY TWENTY-THREE, AND NOT STONED UNLESS THE FIRST THREE ARE THERE. "A GLUTTON AND A DRUNKARD" — OF MEAT AND OF WINE; THOUGH NO PROOF, A REMEMBRANCE: "BE NOT AMONG WINE-DRINKERS, AMONG GLUTTONS OF MEAT" (PROVERBS 23:20-21). ({SP_(219, 4, "גדם", "או", "חגר", "או", "אלם", "או", "סומה", "או", "חרש")} "maimed or lame or mute or blind or deaf"; {SP_(219, 4, "מתרים", "בו", "בפני", "שלשה", "ומלקים", "אותו")} "they warn him before three and flog him"; {SP_(219, 4, "חזר", "וקלקל", "נדון", "בעשרים", "ושלש")} "if he repeated and sinned he is judged by twenty-three"; {SP_(219, 4, "זולל", "בבשר", "וסובא", "ביין")} "a glutton of meat and a drunkard of wine"): THE PARENTS\' FIVE ABILITIES READ FROM THE FIVE VERBS, THE TWO COURTS (three, then twenty-three with the first three present) and THE OBJECTS meat and wine (Sanhedrin 8:4 the answer sheet, the whole row the Mishnah\'s) — the compile\'s parent-ability conditions, the two-trial sequence, the Proverbs remembrance a case, never a row. Fresh.')
srow(220, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND ALL THE MEN OF HIS CITY SHALL STONE HIM" (21:21) — DO ALL THE MEN OF HIS CITY STONE HIM? RATHER, IN THE PRESENCE OF ALL THE MEN OF HIS CITY. ({SP_(220, 1, "וכי", "כל", "אנשי", "עירו", "רוגמים", "אותו")} "do all the men of his city stone him"; {SP_(220, 1, "אלא", "במעמד", "כל", "אנשי", "עירו")} "rather, in the presence of all the men of his city"): "all" a presence, not an act (the witnesses\' hand first, 17:7 — chapters 17-18) — the compile\'s stoning cell REFERENCED with the presence condition. Fresh.')
srow(220, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"WITH STONES" — MIGHT IT BE MANY STONES? "WITH A STONE" (LEVITICUS 20:2). MIGHT IT BE ONE STONE? "WITH STONES" — IF HE DID NOT DIE BY THE FIRST, HE DIES BY THE SECOND. ({SP_(220, 2, "יכול", "באבנים", "מרבות")} "might it be with many stones"; {SP_(220, 2, "יכול", "באבן", "אחת")} "might it be with one stone"; {SP_(220, 2, "לא", "מת", "בראשונה", "ימות", "בשניה")} "if he did not die by the first, he dies by the second"): THE STONING\'S MANNER — one stone, then more (Sanhedrin 6:4 the answer sheet; the same reading at 13:11 — 13\'s piska, the English\'s parallels) — the compile\'s stoning cell REFERENCED. Fresh.')
srow(220, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'R. YOSE SAID: BECAUSE HE ATE A TARTEMAR OF MEAT AND DRANK HALF A LOG OF WINE, IS HE STONED? RATHER THE TORAH REACHED THE END OF HIS MATTER AND SAID: LET HIM DIE INNOCENT AND NOT DIE GUILTY. FOR THE DEATH OF THE WICKED IS A BENEFIT TO THEM AND TO THE WORLD, AND OF THE RIGHTEOUS AN EVIL TO THEM AND TO THE WORLD. ({SP_(220, 3, "תרטימר", "בשר", "ושתה", "חצי", "לוג", "יין")} "a tartemar of meat and drank half a log of wine"; {SP_(220, 3, "ימות", "זכי", "ואל", "ימות", "חיב")} "let him die innocent and not die guilty"; {SP_(220, 3, "שמיתתם", "של", "רשעים", "הניה", "להם", "והניה", "לעולם")} "that the death of the wicked is a benefit to them and to the world"): THE MEASURES NAMED IN THE SPINE\'S HEBREW — a tartemar (half a maneh) of meat, half a log of wine (Sanhedrin 8:2 the answer sheet\'s parameters) and the rationale (8:5) — the compile\'s two thresholds read here. Fresh.')
srow(220, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL PURGE THE EVIL" — PURGE THE DOERS OF EVIL FROM ISRAEL. ({SP_(220, 4, "בער", "עושי", "הרעות", "מישראל")} "purge the doers of evil from Israel"): THE PURGE FORMULA\'S FIFTH SEAT (13:6, 17:7, 17:12, 19:19, 21:21 — the walk\'s count) read as persons as at 210:9 — the compile\'s effect. Fresh.')
srow(221, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND WHEN A MAN HAS A SIN OF A DEATH SENTENCE AND IS PUT TO DEATH" (21:22) — A MAN IS HANGED, A WOMAN IS NOT HANGED; R. ELIEZER SAYS: A WOMAN TOO IS HANGED. ({SP_(221, 1, "האיש", "נתלה", "ואין", "האשה", "נתלית")} "the man is hanged and the woman is not hanged"; {SP_(221, 1, "אף", "האשה", "נתלית")} "the woman too is hanged"): THE HANGING\'S SEX CONDITION (Sanhedrin 6:4 the answer sheet, R. Eliezer\'s dissent) — the compile\'s parameter with the dispute. Fresh.')
srow(221, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'R. ELIEZER SAID TO THEM: DID NOT SHIMON B. SHETACH HANG WOMEN IN ASHKELON? THEY SAID: HE HANGED EIGHTY WOMEN, AND TWO ARE NOT JUDGED IN ONE DAY — RATHER THE HOUR REQUIRED IT, TO TEACH OTHERS. ({SP_(221, 2, "שמעון", "בן", "שטח", "תלה", "נשים", "באשקלון")} "Shimon b. Shetach hanged women in Ashkelon"; {SP_(221, 2, "שמונים", "נשים", "תלה")} "eighty women he hanged"; {SP_(221, 2, "ואין", "דנים", "שנים", "ביום", "אחד")} "and two are not judged in one day"; {SP_(221, 2, "שהשעה", "צריכה", "ללמד", "בה", "את", "אחרים")} "that the hour required it, to teach others"): THE PRECEDENT DISMISSED AS AN EMERGENCY MEASURE — and the rule "not two in one day" (221:4) stated inside the answer (Sanhedrin 6:4) — the compile\'s one-a-day parameter; the row without a citation. Fresh.')
srow(221, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL HANG HIM" — MIGHT ALL THE STONED BE HANGED? "FOR A HANGED ONE IS A CURSE OF GOD" (21:23) — AFTER INCLUDING, THE VERSE EXCLUDED: WE LEARN FROM THE REVILER — AS THE REVILER STRETCHED HIS HAND AGAINST THE ROOT AND IS HANGED, SO ALL WHO STRETCH THEIR HAND AGAINST THE ROOT ARE HANGED; R. ELIEZER: AS THE REVILER IS STONED AND HANGED, SO ALL THE STONED ARE HANGED. MIGHT THEY HANG HIM ALIVE AS THE KINGDOM DOES? "AND HE IS PUT TO DEATH AND YOU HANG HIM". ({SP_(221, 3, "יכול", "יהו", "כל", "הנסקלים", "נתלים")} "might all the stoned be hanged"; {SP_(221, 3, "אחר", "שרבה", "הכתוב", "מיעט")} "after the verse included it excluded"; {SP_(221, 3, "שפשט", "ידו", "בעקר")} "who stretched his hand against the root"; {SP_(221, 3, "כך", "כל", "הנסקלים", "נתלים")} "so all the stoned are hanged"; {SP_(221, 3, "תולים", "אותו", "חי", "כדרך", "שהמלכות", "עושה")} "hang him alive as the kingdom does"): WHO IS HANGED — the reviler and the idolater (the sages) or all the stoned (R. Eliezer) — Sanhedrin 6:4 the answer sheet; the hanging AFTER death (not the kingdom\'s crucifixion — Onkelos\'s gibbet word) — the compile\'s class parameter with the dispute and the sequence death → hanging. Fresh.')
srow(221, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"HIM" — AND NOT HIS GARMENTS; "HIM" — AND NOT HIS WITNESSES; "HIM" — AND NOT HIS PLOTTERS; "HIM" — AND NOT TWO IN ONE DAY. ({SP_(221, 4, "אתו", "ולא", "את", "כליו")} "him and not his garments"; {SP_(221, 4, "ולא", "את", "עדיו")} "and not his witnesses"; {SP_(221, 4, "ולא", "את", "זוממיו")} "and not his plotters"; {SP_(221, 4, "ולא", "שנים", "ביום", "אחד")} "and not two in one day"): THE FOUR EXCLUSIONS OF "HIM" — the plotting witnesses (19:19\'s "as he plotted") are not hanged though executed — the compile\'s scope: the hanging one man, one day (221:2\'s rule; the row without a citation). Fresh.')
srow(221, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"ON A TREE" — MIGHT IT BE AN UPROOTED TREE OR AN ATTACHED ONE? "YOU SHALL SURELY BURY HIM" (21:23) — ON A TREE BURIED WITH HIM: THE UPROOTED, NOT THE ATTACHED. ({SP_(221, 5, "בעץ", "התלוש", "או", "בעץ", "המחבר")} "on an uprooted tree or on an attached tree"; {SP_(221, 5, "בעץ", "שנקבר", "עמו")} "on a tree that is buried with him"): THE GIBBET BURIED WITH HIM — the tree detached (Sanhedrin 6:4: a beam sunk in the ground) — the compile\'s instrument parameter. Fresh.')
srow(221, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE THAT ONE WHO LEAVES HIS DEAD OVERNIGHT TRANSGRESSES A PROHIBITION? "HIS CORPSE SHALL NOT STAY THE NIGHT ON THE TREE". LEFT HIM FOR HIS HONOR, TO BRING A COFFIN AND SHROUDS — TRANSGRESSES? "ON THE TREE": AS THE TREE IS HIS DISGRACE, SO ANYTHING THAT IS HIS DISGRACE; OUT GOES THE ONE WHO LEAVES HIM FOR HIS HONOR. ({SP_(221, 6, "למלין", "את", "מתו", "שהוא", "עובר", "בלא", "תעשה")} "one who leaves his dead overnight transgresses a prohibition"; {SP_(221, 6, "הלינו", "לכבודו", "להביא", "לו", "ארון", "ותכריכים")} "left him overnight for his honor, to bring him a coffin and shrouds"; {SP_(221, 6, "שהוא", "נוול", "לו")} "that it is a disgrace to him"): THE OVERNIGHT BAR EXTENDED TO EVERY DEAD (Sanhedrin 6:5 the answer sheet) WITH THE HONOR EXCEPTION — the compile\'s burial law for all the dead, the delay for honor permitted. Fresh.')
srow(221, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"HIS CORPSE SHALL NOT STAY THE NIGHT" — A PROHIBITION; "YOU SHALL SURELY BURY HIM" — A COMMAND. HOW DO THEY DO IT? THEY WAIT FOR HIM UNTIL DUSK, HANG HIM AND RELEASE HIM; IF HE STAYED THE NIGHT THEY TRANSGRESS. ({SP_(221, 7, "מצות", "לא", "תעשה")} "a prohibition"; {SP_(221, 7, "מצות", "עשה")} "a command"; {SP_(221, 7, "ממתינים", "לו", "עד", "חשכה", "ותולים", "לו", "ומתירים", "אותו")} "they wait for him until dusk, hang him and release him"; {SP_(221, 7, "ואם", "לן", "עוברים", "עליו", "בלא", "תעשה")} "and if he stayed the night they transgress a prohibition"): THE HANGING AT DUSK, THE RELEASE AT ONCE (Sanhedrin 6:4: "one ties and one unties") — the compile\'s clock on the hanging: the day\'s end, the same day\'s burial. Fresh.')
srow(221, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR A HANGED ONE IS A CURSE OF GOD" — WHY IS THIS ONE HANGED? BECAUSE HE CURSED THE NAME, AND THE NAME OF HEAVEN IS FOUND PROFANED. ({SP_(221, 8, "מפני", "מה", "זה", "תלוי")} "why is this one hanged"; {SP_(221, 8, "מפני", "שקלל", "את", "השם")} "because he cursed the Name"; {SP_(221, 8, "ונמצא", "שם", "שמים", "מתחלל")} "and the Name of Heaven is found profaned"): THE CURSE IS THE REVILER\'S, the display a profanation (Sanhedrin 6:4\'s reason for the brief hanging) — Onkelos writes the cause "because he sinned before the LORD" (the ink\'s find 4) — the compile\'s rationale. Fresh.')
srow(221, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'THE MAN IS STONED NAKED, THE WOMAN IS NOT STONED NAKED. R. JUDAH SAYS: BOTH, BUT THE MAN IS HANGED FACING THE PEOPLE, THE WOMAN FACING THE TREE; THE MAN ONE CLOTH IN FRONT, THE WOMAN TWO, FOR ALL OF HER IS NAKEDNESS. ({SP_(221, 9, "האיש", "נסקל", "ערום", "ואין", "האשה", "נסקלת", "ערומה")} "the man is stoned naked and the woman is not stoned naked"; {SP_(221, 9, "ופניו", "כלפי", "העם", "ואחוריו", "כלפי", "העץ")} "and his face toward the people and his back toward the tree"; {SP_(221, 9, "סרט", "אחד", "מלפניו")} "one cloth in front of him"; {SP_(221, 9, "שני", "סרטים")} "two cloths"; {SP_(221, 9, "מפני", "שכלה", "ערוה")} "because all of her is nakedness"): THE STONED\'S COVERING (Sanhedrin 6:3 the answer sheet, R. Judah\'s dissent) and R. Judah\'s hanging of the woman by posture — the compile\'s note, the row without a citation. Fresh.')
srow(221, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL NOT DEFILE YOUR LAND WHICH THE LORD YOUR GOD GIVES YOU AS AN INHERITANCE" — TO WARN THE COURT ABOUT THIS. ({SP_(221, 10, "להזהיר", "בית", "דין", "על", "כך")} "to warn the court about this"): THE COURT THE ADDRESSEE (171:1\'s trope, the English) — the burial\'s duty the court\'s; the gift formula\'s seat 21:23 (the computed twelve, 15b) — the compile\'s addressee. Fresh.')
